  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mutomo Integrated Sustainable Livelihoods Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve the food security of up to 450 farming households in Mutomo. Mutomo district is an ASAL district in Eastern Province. Specifically, participating farmers are located in Makele, Nduudune and Kianga sub-locations, Ikanga location, Ikanga division, Mutomo. 

The main project activities are:
1. promotion of high value drought tolerant crop species and varieties through crop production.
2. Agro-forestry by introducing tree planting and fruit tree nurseries as an income generating activity and the creation of awareness on climatic changes.
3. Promotion and/or multiplication of gala goats.
4. Enhancement of natural resource management through soil and water conservation by construction of soil structures using a catchments approach.</narrative>
  </description>
